{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וזאת תורת האשם", :translit "v'zot torat ha-asham", :gloss "and this is the law of the guilt-offering"} {:he "אשם", :translit "asham", :gloss "guilt-offering"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["אשם"]}], :frame {:text "The Torah designates five specific scenarios that obligate a person to bring an asham offering: (1) failure to fulfill an oath (Leviticus 5:15–16); (2) inadvertent sacrilege of consecrated property (Leviticus 5:17–19); (3) uncertain whether one committed a sin whose penalty is karet (Leviticus 5:20–26); (4) theft or false oath with subsequent confession (Leviticus 5:20–26); and (5) the asham of a nazirite who became defiled (Numbers 6:10–12). These are enumerated in tractate Keritot as the five obligatory asham offerings.", :sources ["Keritot 2a" "Leviticus 5:15–26" "Numbers 6:10–12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["אשם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "אשם", :refs ["Genesis 26:10" "Leviticus 5:19" "Leviticus 7:5" "Leviticus 14:21" "Leviticus 19:21" "Numbers 5:7" "1 Samuel 6:3" "1 Samuel 6:8"], :n 14, :lens :exact}]}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:14.993286629Z", :model "glm-5.2"}